# Overwatch — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values. `.env.local` is git-ignored and never
# leaves your machine; this file lists only the names, so it is safe to commit.
#
# Every one of these is read on the server. None of them is prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_, which is what
# would put a value into the JavaScript the browser downloads — so no key here ever reaches a
# browser, yours or anyone else's.

# The password for the whole app. Anything without a valid session cookie gets a 401, including
# the API, so this is the only thing standing between the internet and your journal. Set it to
# something long. In production the app refuses to serve at all if this is unset, rather than
# quietly running open.
APP_PASSWORD=

# A second password, in front of the Portfolio page only. Optional: leave it blank and the page
# behaves like every other one. When set, the page locks itself every time you navigate away, so
# coming back means typing this again. Make it different from APP_PASSWORD — a second copy of the
# same password is not a second lock.
#
# What this is for: keeping your net worth off the screen when someone glances at an already
# signed-in browser. Anyone who knows APP_PASSWORD is already inside the app, so this is a second
# thing to know, not a second layer of encryption.
PORTFOLIO_PASSWORD=

# Historical futures candles for backtesting. Optional: without it, replay uses whatever is
# already stored in market.db and new imports fail with a clear message.
DATABENTO_API_KEY=

# Live prices for the Portfolio page — https://finnhub.io, free tier is 60 calls/minute.
# Optional: without it the portfolio still works from cost basis and any prices already cached,
# and the page says prices are unavailable rather than showing stale numbers as current.
FINNHUB_API_KEY=

# Where the databases and uploads live. Defaults to ./data. On a hosted deployment set this to
# the mounted volume so your data survives a redeploy.
# TJ_DATA_DIR=/data
